{
  "schema": "pdf-struct/toolcompare/1",
  "note": "Routes run over the whole document (no --pages probe). naive = PyMuPDF page.get_text('text'). pymupdf4llm = pymupdf4llm 2.1 to_markdown(doc, use_ocr=False), every other argument at library default (table_strategy='lines_strict'); OCR is off because no OCR engine is installed offline. skill = outputs/scripts/parse_pdf.py (pdf-struct/2): heading/table/block counts read from results/<name>/report.json (stats.n_sections, n_tables, n_blocks), body text from a regenerated run in work/_tools_probe/engine/<name> whose stats are asserted equal to the shipped report.json. Geometry helpers (_lines_of_page, _col_of, two-column gate) are copied from baseline_compare.py. running_header_lines_leaked: header set per PDF = engine dropped_running_text (len>=8, non-numeric) UNION lines in the top/bottom 10% repeated on >=3 pages; the same set is applied to all three tools, a hit is a full-line match after whitespace normalisation. figure_label_chars_leaked: inventory = chars of engine blocks typed figure_label; a label (>=4 chars, so body numbers cannot fake a match) counts when it appears on that same page of the tool's output and is not explainable by a non-figure block of that page. Two honest caveats, both visible in diag: (1) the running-header metric only fires on vit -- the other four PDFs carry page numbers only in their margins, and bare numbers are excluded by design, so 0 there means 'no qualifying running head', not 'measured clean'; (2) gpt3 has an empty figure_label inventory (its figures are vector charts without typed labels), so its figure value of 0 means 'nothing to leak' -- diag marks it figure_metric_applicable=false. cross_column_interleavings: scored only for document-level 2-column PDFs (resnet, bert) with baseline's gate (gutter <=12% of content width, >=8 units in each band); the unit is the tool's own emitted unit (line for naive/pymupdf4llm, paragraph block for skill) and units straddling the gutter are skipped; null = not applicable, never zero. In results/baseline.json the skill side of that metric was 0 by construction (the engine's own block order); here it is re-measured from the emitted text.md with the same rule, which is why it is not exactly 0. wall_time_s: naive and pymupdf4llm are the median of 3 full runs in one process; skill is the median of 3 end-to-end CLI runs from results/perf.json when present (that CLI run also rasterises figures and overlay PNGs, which the other two do not), else one run. n/a = not computable.",
